{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #126: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that if $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}$ has $\\lvert A\\rvert=n$ then $\\prod_{a\\neq b\\in A}(a+b)$ has at least $f(n)$ distinct prime factors. Is it true that $f(n)/\\log n\\to\\infty$? Current best: Investigated by Erd\\H{o}s and Tur\\'{a}n \\cite{ErTu34} (prompted by a question of L\\'{a}z\\'{a}r and Gr\\\"{u}nwald) in their first joint paper, where they proved that\\[\\log n \\ll f(n) \\ll n/\\log n\\](the upper bound is trivial, taking $A=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$). Prize: $250. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_636ef0b3c369887e40aef7fae6fbb116f079c938822e00762357fd7cb645f380","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:126","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_dc157a906240142d","object_root":"sha256:e953d878d5557b0a28b56f94e6ee45c5653255b9369332ec642bb261fe2fb0a6","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:126"}],"rel